    codeLanguage: "xml",
    code: "<PropertyGroup>\n  <TargetFramework>net8.0-windows</TargetFramework>\n  <ImplicitUsings>enable</ImplicitUsings>\n  <Nullable>enable</Nullable>\n  <IsTestProject>true</IsTestProject>\n  <UseWindowsForms>true</UseWindowsForms>\n</PropertyGroup>\n\n<ItemGroup>\n  <PackageReference Include=\"Allure.NUnit\" Version=\"2.15.0\" />\n  <PackageReference Include=\"FlaUI.Core\" Version=\"5.0.0\" />\n  <PackageReference Include=\"FlaUI.UIA3\" Version=\"5.0.0\" />\n  <PackageReference Include=\"Microsoft.NET.Test.Sdk\" Version=\"18.9.0\" />\n  <PackageReference Include=\"NUnit\" Version=\"4.6.1\" />\n  <PackageReference Include=\"NUnit3TestAdapter\" Version=\"6.3.0\" />\n</ItemGroup>",
    what: "MSBuild reads this file before compilation. The Windows target framework enables Windows-specific APIs, `IsTestProject` marks the project as tests, Windows Forms support is needed for clipboard/input-language helpers, and the package references provide the test SDK/adapter, NUnit API, FlaUI core/UIA3 implementation and Allure integration.",
    whatUk: "MSBuild читає цей file до compilation. Windows target framework вмикає Windows-specific APIs, `IsTestProject` позначає project як tests, Windows Forms support потрібен для clipboard/input-language helpers, а package references дають test SDK/adapter, NUnit API, FlaUI core/UIA3 implementation та Allure integration.",
    why: "Unlike Python's `requirements.txt`, the project file also controls compilation/runtime features. It is both dependency declaration and build configuration.",
